    id: 'architecture-collaboration',
    title: 'Shared work and remote execution',
    summary:
      'How shared documents, presence, execution placement, and machine-local state fit together—and which proofs remain separate.',
    body: 'How shared documents, presence, execution placement, and machine-local state fit together—and which proofs remain separate.\n\nThis is a reading path through shipped documentation, not live state or a completed semantic audit.\n\nQuestions:\n- Which facts are portable, and which belong to one Station home?\n- Does presence imply permission to edit or execute?\n- How is a possibly accepted remote effect reconciled after disconnection?\n\nRead module topics with get_station_docs_topic:\n- architecture-sharedworkingstate: SharedWorkingState\n- architecture-liveworksession: LiveWorkSession\n- architecture-sharedworkingstateeditingcapability: SharedWorkingStateEditingCapability\n- architecture-cloud-move-preparation: Cloud move preparation\n- architecture-evidence-gated-and-retained-internal-work: Evidence-gated and retained internal work\n\nCanonical reading:\n- docs/design/shared-working-state.md\n- docs/design/live-work-session.md\n- docs/guides/machine-relationships.md\n- docs/guides/home-transfer-controller.md\n- docs/reference/project-task-room-collaboration-acceptance.md',
