    summary:
      'How extensions declare contributions, receive grants, activate capabilities, and call Station through published contracts.',
    body: 'How extensions declare contributions, receive grants, activate capabilities, and call Station through published contracts.\n\nThis is a reading path through shipped documentation, not live state or a completed semantic audit.\n\nQuestions:\n- Is installed the same as admitted, granted, or active?\n- What can be withdrawn safely while work is running?\n- Does a plugin depend on a public contract or reach into an implementation?\n\nRead module topics with get_station_docs_topic:\n- architecture-registry-trust-policy-decisions: Registry trust policy decisions\n- architecture-agentpluginloader: AgentPluginLoader\n- architecture-packagemcpadmissionjournal: PackageMcpAdmissionJournal\n- architecture-installedplugininventory: InstalledPluginInventory\n- architecture-pluginforegroundruns: PluginForegroundRuns\n- architecture-plugincompositionmodule: PluginCompositionModule\n- architecture-plugingrantreconciliation: PluginGrantReconciliation\n- architecture-registrysupplychainpolicy: RegistrySupplyChainPolicy\n- architecture-localskillmutationauthority-and-setupimporteffectjournal: LocalSkillMutationAuthority and SetupImportEffectJournal\n\nCanonical reading:\n- docs/guides/plugins.md\n- docs/reference/contracts.md\n- docs/reference/sdk.md\n- examples/README.md\n- docs/guides/distribution-profiles.md',
    tags: ['architecture', 'extensions'],
