    summary:
      'How a result is tied to a revision, what a gate actually proves, and how a missing proof remains visible.',
    body: 'How a result is tied to a revision, what a gate actually proves, and how a missing proof remains visible.\n\nThis is a reading path through shipped documentation, not live state or a completed semantic audit.\n\nQuestions:\n- Does this receipt match the exact work and revision being claimed?\n- Is a passing check behavioral proof or only a structural guard?\n- Which claims still require a real provider, Device, or hosted run?\n\nRead module topics with get_station_docs_topic:\n- architecture-revisionevidencemodule: RevisionEvidenceModule\n- architecture-actionoperationmodule: ActionOperationModule\n- architecture-reviewevidencemodule: ReviewEvidenceModule\n- architecture-verificationcoordinator: VerificationCoordinator\n- architecture-browser-test-evidence: Browser test evidence\n\nCanonical reading:\n- docs/guides/testing.md\n- docs/reference/verification-receipts.md\n- .veritas/README.md\n- docs/guides/documentation.md\n- docs/plans/documentation-code-audit.md',
